IMPORT prelude

-- Long Service Leave Act 1981 (NT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts in completed years of continuous service (ss 8, 10), in months
-- ("not less than 2 months notice", s 8(7); "re-employed ... within 2 months", s 12(4)(e); "within a period of 12 months
-- after completing that apprenticeship", s 12(3); "not later than 12 months after his or her death", s 11(7)(b)) and in
-- years ("until the expiration of 3 years", "6 years after", s 14(2); "within 3 years after the act or omission", s 18A).
--
-- A period of months or years after a day ends on the same day of the month that many months or years later; where that
-- month has no such day (31 August + 1 month; 29 February in a common year), on the last day of that month (fork F1).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY. Quotations are from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Northern Territory's Word
-- reprint REPL021 of the Long Service Leave Act 1981, not an official version. Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Long Service Leave Act 1981 (NT)`

-- A date written day, month, year.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Whether the first day is earlier than the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- Whether the first day is the second day or earlier.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is on or before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH IF m EQUALS 2 THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
           IF m EQUALS 4 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 6 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 9 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

-- The same day of the month, n calendar months later (clamped to the last day of a shorter month; fork F1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `months counted from year 0` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year` MEANS FLOOR (`months counted from year 0` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month` MEANS (`months counted from year 0` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`
            THEN `the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`

-- The same day of the month, n calendar years later.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` n `years after` `the start` MEANS `the same day` (n TIMES 12) `months after` `the start`

-- The number of whole years completed from a first day of service to a last day of service, both days counted (fork F2):
-- a year is complete when the day after the last day reaches the anniversary of the first day. Service from 1 January 2015
-- to 31 December 2024 is 10 completed years.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the completed years from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the last day` `is before` `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the anniversary is reached`
         THEN `the difference in years`
         ELSE `the difference in years` MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `the day after` MEANS `the date` 1 `days after` `the last day`
        `the difference in years` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day after` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the first day`
        `the anniversary is reached` MEANS
                (DATE_MONTH `the day after` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `the first day`)
            OR  (    (DATE_MONTH `the day after` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `the first day`)
                 AND (DATE_DAY `the day after` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `the first day`))
